    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Cry is the thirteenth studio album of original material by Scottish rock band Simple Minds, released in April 2002 on Eagle Records. It was recorded in late 2001 in Sicily and Glasgow, with Jim Kerr driving much of the songwriting and production, and it marked a return to a more focused, melody-led form after the band’s late-1990s experimentation.\n\nMusically, the album blends electronic textures with rock dynamics, combining polished synth layers, programmed beats, and atmospheric arrangements with Kerr’s mature vocals and Charlie Burchill’s guitar work. Songs such as “Cry,” “Spaceface,” and “New Sunshine Morning” highlight its sleek, emotionally direct style, while the record as a whole was generally heard as a contemporary comeback that balanced a modern production sheen with the band’s familiar anthemic instincts.",
